<p><strong>A salon appointment app lets clients book online by branch, service and stylist at any hour, while you see every booking in one calendar. For a salon or beauty parlour in Nepal it replaces phone calls, WhatsApp messages and the paper register, and it stops two clients being booked with the same stylist at the same time.</strong></p>
<p>Many salons in Kathmandu, Lalitpur and Pokhara still take bookings through calls and chat. That works until a busy Saturday, a missed message or a second branch. An appointment app fixes the booking itself, and the better ones also tidy up what happens after.</p>
<h2>What clients see</h2>
<p>Clients open a link on their phone, pick the branch, the service and the stylist, choose a free time and confirm. There is nothing to install. The booking lands in the salon calendar straight away, so the front desk is not copying messages into a diary.</p>
<h2>What the salon gets</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>One calendar.</strong> Every stylist and branch in one view, with no double-bookings. See <a href="/features/booking/">how Zennly books</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Fewer no-shows.</strong> Confirmations and reminders give clients an easy way to keep or change a time.</li>
<li><strong>A payment record.</strong> Cash, card and online payments logged against each booking. See <a href="/features/payment-tracking/">payment tracking</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Discount control.</strong> Discounts requested, approved and recorded. See <a href="/features/discount-management/">discount management</a>.</li>
</ul>
<h2>What to check before you choose an app</h2>
<p>Ask whether it handles several branches, whether stylists can have different hours and services, and whether the owner can see revenue across locations without phoning each manager. Ask to see it with real services, not a blank demo. Our <a href="/blog/best-salon-software-nepal/">salon software buying guide</a> lists the questions to ask every vendor.</p>
